280258b1",5,-5,0,"do we have a different bug specific for 3.2 migration, do we need a separate list for easier tracking the fixes"]],0,3],[8131485,20662,319,6.536,5.29,[[10,0.115,0,38],[11,0.068,0,22],[12,0.062,0,20],[13,0.059,0,19],[14,0.056,0,18],[15,0.056,0,18],[16,0.053,0,17],[17,0.053,0,17],[18,0.05,0,16],[19,0.05,0,16],[20,0.05,0,16],[21,0.05,0,16],[22,0.05,0,16],[23,0.044,0,14],[24,0.038,0,12],[25,0.036,0,11],[26,0.036,0,11],[27,0.036,0,11],[28,0.036,0,11]],[],0,4],[8131922,20662,27,0.662,0.495,[[29,0]],[],0,5],[8131147,20662,31,0.662,0.495,[[30,0]],[],0,6],[8131923,20663,72,2.202,1.731,[[31,0]],[],0,7],[8174323,20669,91,2.202,1.731,[[32,0.667,0,61],[33,0.302,0,28],[34,0.031,0,2]],[["238cf76c_68f87b43",6,-5,1,"Check host_os and host_cpu here instead?"],["23c3942d_a995c4d2",6,-5,1,"Do you check that you can conditionally set script_executable in .gn for these different python path?"],["2c964ade_35aa27f6",6,-5,1,"Better to use variable for version?"],["4a3abc78_a86acf9c",6,-5,1,"We also want to download linux-amd64 package even in non-linux host OS too to send the files to remote workers."],["5cc4ac23_8fec5c3e",6,-5,1,"Sorry, you need to use ${{platform}} like https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:DEPS;l=1168;drc=16a88fbabc5f6594ee038e6b288f8e96393b787f"],["720fc36a_39ec1e5c",6,-5,0,"We have an option to put a Python wrapper at `third_party/cpython3/python3` and `third/party/cpython3/python3.bat`, which finds the corresponding Python path depending on the runtime. e.g. Choose…"],["9eef59fe_afb32a89",7,-5,1,"sort here?"],["bcedddae_9f804f38",6,-5,0,"Unifing these by using $platform is still simpler than having conditional checks in each place where we specify hermetic python path?"],["d24bb92f_c6e91882",6,-5,1,"Could you add README in this directory as written in https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/adding_to_third_party.md#standard-dep-structure ?"],["02cd5221_bd37b505",1,-4,1,"Duplicated footer?"],["2cee1ce4_85079e65",6,-4,0,"How big is this? Do we have a gclient var for turning off downloads for things needed only for siso?"],["8459a4cd_10fc8844",7,-4,1,"nit: this shouldn't be necessary since you already have \"Shipped: No\" in the README.chromium."],["d953fcd5_a8887550",1,-4,1,"I think it is better to write why you make these changes rather than just writing what does this CL do."],["4ad8bec3_a22bb50a",6,-1,1,"nit: other places have {linux-amd64, mac-arm64, windows-amd64....} paths instead of `host`. I prefer that to be aligned. An advantage would be that you don't fetch two CIPD packages at different…"],["629c89f7_5fc8650f",8,-1,0,"I've checked and this license is good to use, but it will need to be added to the license allowlist. I've created http://crrev.com/c/8184755 to do this."],["b3e35099_2f4a9c05",8,-1,0,"Can you please file a bug for an autoroll exception? https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/adding_to_third_party.md#update-mechanism"],["21d1a47a_91e74bce",9,0,1,"Why do you need this change?"],["921d512f_f803c255",6,0,0,"```suggestion # Python package used by GN and build steps. Since we can't conditionally set `script_executable`, # we use the same python path for different platforms. ```"],["9b05ff0a_a0419597",1,0,1,"Better to add 541940412 as well?"]],0,8],[8171523,20672,237,3.848,3.085,[[35,1.0,0,243]],[],0,9],[8171524,20675,150,3.848,3.085,[[36,0]],[["bd7099e0_f0881d31",10,-3,0,"Hmm, is this intentional?"]],0,10],[8220748,20675,8,0.399,0.286,[[37,0]],[["f60a4300_cdf10a6b",2,-3,0,"Does this run for the dirs with yapf? How fast would it be?"],["628b4a29_bb86d1b3",2,0,0,"Do we need to have this in every PRESUBMIT.py instead of only in build/PRESUBMIT.py ?"]],0,11],[8190675,20675,79,2.202,1.731,[[32,0.762,1,61],[33,0.202,1,16],[34,0.036,1,2]],[["3d40fe6b_66fab5a0",11,-5,1,"Update this path."],["8de4586e_89547603",6,-5,1,"Now, there is meaningless \"host\" in the path, which is confusing because there is no counterpart \"remote\" python."],["a12fa621_dca04aa9",11,-5,1,"Update this?"],["bd313e61_c34fa2bc",6,-5,1,"nit: It's actually GN, not Siso."],["d4568a95_401ee107",11,-5,1,"Please fix this, too."],["e215666a_5d922ea7",6,-5,1,"I think it is better to have subdirectory for CIPD package extraction."],["eacfa1d6_1ff1527e",8,-5,1,"This explanation doesn't make sense now."],["21b63e1f_4cf58cd2",1,0,0,"Better to use publically accessible link like https://crrev.com/c/8212559"],["f2ac4bf1_3e1b271f",1,0,1,"Could you leave link to CL doing this as a reference?"]],0,13],[8229169,20677,12,0.389,0.248,[[33,1]],[],0,13],[8253938,20678,149,3.848,3.085,[[8,0.956,2,143],[37,0.044,2,6]],[],0,14],[8255589,20678,140,3.848,3.085,[[38,0]],[],0,15],[8255450,20678,544,9.231,7.843,[[39,1.0,0,548]],[],0,17],[8256249,20678,1,0.087,0.066,[[33,2]],[],0,18],[8255001,20678,275,6.365,5.17,[[40,0]],[],0,19],[8255230,20678,1830,8.899,7.191,[[0,0.872,1,1603],[41,0.109,0,201],[42,0.019,0,34]],[],0,21],[8256113,20679,142,3.848,3.085,[[43,0]],[],0,23],[8160801,20679,222,1.6,0.886,[[44,0.938,1,211],[33,0.025,3,5],[45,0.012,1,2],[46,0.012,1,2],[47,0.012,1,2]],[["6cc7998d_91fe0697",12,-15,1,"I think it is better to set this directly in remote_command of each rule as default value of remote_command won't be used if we have this here?"],["7f77a05e_0032dfd6",1,-15,1,"This is not done in this CL?"],["a3134967_9379cbf6",13,-15,1,"Can you update the DEPS to install CPython?"],["bfc1cbdb_33949900",12,-15,1,"Update script_executable in `.gn` to use the same python version between local and remote build? And then checking only platform.python_bin is sufficient here?"],["c279f2c0_9c624f11",1,-15,1,"This doesn't happen in this CL?"],["d6e69e0f_c6dd7dec",13,-15,1,"We are going to replace them to `third_party/cpython3/{platform}/bin/python3` (or .exe), right? Can you leave a TODO?"],["dc39f2fe_caca92c1",13,-15,1,"Is it possible to add the python inputs automatically without manual configuration like https://crrev.com/c/8173823?"],["169ced7a_b5b79095",13,-14,1,"Using if statement might be bit simpler than a dict lookup here? ```suggestion __python_bin = \"third_party/cpython3/host/bin/python3\" + (.exe\" if runtime.os == \"windows\" else \"\") ```"],["30fc13e5_a86d0f7d",12,-14,1,"I think it is fine to have filegroups.update here instead of per OS file."],["57834094_b4b108d6",13,-14,1,"ditto"],["6bf2f1b1_13b0cc70",12,-14,1,"Some python action still cannot run remotely, so we need to apply this inputs addition only when remote_command is set to platform.remote_python_bin"],["770a5716_70cd4eb7",12,-14,1,"This is not necessary?"],["b85bc0a3_73ca6a52",13,-14,0,"Upload files only under remote dir?"],["db241281_137b33c1",12,-14,1,"These are not necessary."],["e4beb661_60e44a06",12,-14,1,"This is redundant?"],["e8316c89_6bf6ce8f",13,-14,1,"I think you need to use relative path from build dir instead of from repository root."],["107006da_3bc4c738",14,-10,1,"I think you need to remove quote in https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni;l=249;drc=67af99cbfc3ed3eb25124d882b64ce87f28f5845 too?"],["d82d89a4_3111fbd1",13,-10,0,"Why windows specific?"],["ca18e00f_c1efba5d",15,-9,0,"I think there are more `\"$python_path\"`. https://source.chromium.org/search?q=language:gn%20%5C%22%5C$python_path%20-file:%5Eout%20-file:%5Egen%20-f:third_party%2Fangle%20-f:third_party&sq= Btw, does…"],["2215e400_5b093371",13,-2,0,"These are not necessary?"],["39273e8d_4adcd765",15,-2,0,"Why revert this?"],["3f4e90fd_b74e9d26",16,-2,1,"Update here."],["41110375_04f9d740",12,-2,0,"Setting this in each rule is sufficient? I think it is better to avoid implicit rewrite of rule config as far as possible to prevent confusion when we faild to find this rewrite."],["944c2885_d97a16b9",12,-2,1,"Doesn't it need to set `remote_command`, instead of checking if the rule has it only when `remote` is true and the command prefix starts with `platform.python_bin`?"],["bcbad1de_466549ba",12,-2,0,"If we specify cpython3 inputs in each rule config, we don't need to have this?"],["f1fda00f_bd613205",12,-2,1,"If we only check `remote_command` is platform.remote_python_bin, this conditional check is not necessary for coverage wrapper command?"],["074fe407_410b3bd4",17,-1,1,"Why not remove quote from https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/toolchain/win/toolchain.gni;l=200;drc=aefa58538d92c224a40e3d0aa7f3c4854804a4b9 too?"],["1415a9ea_b4159688",18,-1,1,"This is not necessary as we use `action` to match the command to run."],["274ba761_017efdc5",12,-1,1,"W/ or w/o this has any change to behavior of this CL?"],["309a2439_d4860da6",12,-1,1,"This is redundant? Or is there any rule which doesn't have remote_command but need to apply input modification?"],["4ec5860d_12450ac4",14,-1,1,"You still need to remvoe this quote from gn config too?"],["50191d13_deabcee3",12,-1,1,"This is redundant? Or is there any rule not having clang_compile_coverage handler but needs to be excluded?"],["5c4fae86_90d2d3c2",12,-1,1,"Better to specify python3 only here to avoid uploading yet another 57MB python3.11 file?"],["5d6ee1e0_de2da902",18,-1,1,"Same."],["88451fa8_21732c2f",12,-1,1,"Better to have this in filegroups of platform.star?"],["8a1fcf20_01c950b6",14,-1,1,"Could you set remote_command for rules using __clang_link handler instead?"],["91a5a939_a4a35870",12,-1,1,"As `include` directory only contains `.h` files, there are not necessary for python script execution?"],["a661ff57_d2e50f6f",13,-1,1,"This doesn't just use go's glob. So can we use `*.py` for lib dir? I made https://crrev.com/c/8256690 to improve documentation."],["a817ea32_f551c7ef",12,-1,1,"Why do we need to send host python?"],["ad511cd6_4a9a748e",12,-1,0,"Can we do like https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/config/siso/typescript_all.star;l=138-148;drc=22e041c69d8b86a7c7290181e531d6f368123446 ?"],["b095749a_125cee19",12,-1,0,"`linux-amd64/lib/**` doens't work?"],["bf511943_d9a4ca14",12,-1,0,"ditto"],[